DECISIONS 213, CODEGEN.md §3.5, §5.3: the ts names depend on the emit's mode (in data and types mode two tables of one record share one id type, their key string), so a ts emit whose mode check refused (E8009) has no name plan to judge: no E8005 idType for those two tables.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A displayed text.
record Label {
  /// Its text.
  text: String
}

/// The names of regions.
let regionNames: table Label = {
  north { text: "North" }
}

/// The names of stages: a second table of the same record.
let stageNames: table Label = {
  first { text: "First" }
}

emit ts { out: "@features/a.ts", mode: zzmode }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8009]  a/a.canon:19:40
  invalid mode zzmode for emit ts: expected one of baked, embedded, data, types

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
